<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yunus Khan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1416–<a href="/years/1487">1487</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yunus Khan was khan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moghulistan">Moghulistan</a> from 1462 to 1487, a Chinggisid ruler of the Chagatai line. Raised in exile among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timurid-empire">Timurids</a>, he was installed with Timurid support and later held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tashkent">Tashkent</a>. His daughter married the Timurid prince Umar Shaikh Mirza, making him the maternal grandfather of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babur">Babur</a>, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/yunus-khan.jpg" alt="Yunus Khan" width="320" height="148" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ro4444 at en.wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Moghulistan.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
